1
00:00:10.599 --> 00:00:13.800
[S01] La plupart de vos décisions n'est même plus votre.

2
00:00:14.199 --> 00:00:17.399
[S01] Avant de parler, vous pensez à la façon dont elle sera écoutée.

3
00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:20.679
[S01] Avant de agir, vous pensez à la façon dont elle sera vue.

4
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:25.000
[S01] Avant de poursuivre ce que vous voulez, vous vous demandez ce que les autres pensent.

5
00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:27.960
[S01] Et petit par petit, sans le remarquer,

6
00:00:28.359 --> 00:00:31.160
[S01] vous transmettez le contrôle de votre vie à des strangers,

7
00:00:31.399 --> 00:00:34.119
[S01] des collègues, des amis, de la famille,

8
00:00:34.359 --> 00:00:36.600
[S01] et des gens qui sont trop occupés avec leurs propres problèmes

9
00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:38.759
[S01] pour penser à vous autant que vous imaginez.

10
00:00:39.479 --> 00:00:42.119
[S01] Vous êtes vivant, mais vous n'avez pas dirigé votre vie.

11
00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:44.280
[S01] Vous manipulez les perceptions.

12
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:48.759
[S01] La vérité difficile est que beaucoup de gens passent leur vie entière en jouant.

13
00:00:49.159 --> 00:00:52.759
[S01] Ils se réveillent, ils mettent en scène la personnalité qui est acceptée,

14
00:00:53.159 --> 00:00:55.079
[S01] ils disent les choses qui gardent la paix,

15
00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:57.159
[S01] ils cachent les parcours qui pourraient être jugés,

16
00:00:57.320 --> 00:00:59.000
[S01] et l'appellent être eux-mêmes.

17
00:00:59.479 --> 00:01:03.799
[S01] De l'extérieur, tout semble normal, peut-être même réussi.

18
00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:06.680
[S01] Mais à l'intérieur, il y a une pression constante,

19
00:01:06.829 --> 00:01:08.280
[S01] une tension constante,

20
00:01:08.359 --> 00:01:12.599
[S01] parce qu'en profondeur, ils savent qu'ils vivent selon leurs attentes au lieu de la vérité.

21
00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:14.750
[S01] C'est pourquoi ils sont exhaustifs.

22
00:01:15.079 --> 00:01:18.439
[S01] Pas parce que la vie est difficile, mais parce que le prétendre est.

23
00:01:18.829 --> 00:01:21.319
[S01] Et voici la vérité que la plupart des gens ne veulent pas entendre.

24
00:01:21.719 --> 00:01:24.840
[S01] Plus vous avez besoin d'approbation, moins libre vous devenez.

25
00:01:25.239 --> 00:01:28.519
[S01] Chaque fois que vous avez besoin de la validation de quelqu'un d'autre pour sentir valable,

26
00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:30.519
[S01] vous abandonnez une partie de votre pouvoir.

27
00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:35.400
[S01] Chaque fois que vous silenciez vous-même pour éviter la rejetion, vous vous trompez.

28
00:01:35.719 --> 00:01:40.200
[S01] Enfin, vous vous réveillez et réalisez que vous avez passé des années à essayer de vous apprécier,

29
00:01:40.359 --> 00:01:43.560
[S01] d'être accepté, compris et apprécié,

30
00:01:43.799 --> 00:01:48.760
[S01] en complètement négligant la seule relation qui détermine la qualité de votre vie entière,

31
00:01:49.159 --> 00:01:50.840
[S01] la relation avec vous-même.

32
00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:54.040
[S01] La plupart des gens ne se perdent pas tous à la fois.

33
00:01:54.359 --> 00:01:57.239
[S01] Ça arrive généralement avec respect, avec paix,

34
00:01:57.480 --> 00:01:59.159
[S01] presque comme les bonnes habitudes.

35
00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:03.480
[S01] Vous apprenez ce qui rend les gens confortables, de sorte que vous deviendrez plus facile à digérer.

36
00:02:03.719 --> 00:02:06.439
[S01] Vous apprenez ce qui est apprécié, de sorte que vous le répétez.

37
00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:09.400
[S01] Vous apprenez ce qui est jugé, de sorte que vous le cachez.

38
00:02:09.719 --> 00:02:14.680
[S01] Petit par petit, votre forme naturelle commence à s'infliger dans les attentes des autres,

39
00:02:14.919 --> 00:02:17.319
[S01] comme un jeune arbre qui croît autour d'un mur.

40
00:02:17.639 --> 00:02:19.319
[S01] Au début, ça semble sans danger.

41
00:02:19.479 --> 00:02:22.430
[S01] Vous êtes juste en adaptant, vous êtes juste réaliste.

42
00:02:22.759 --> 00:02:25.879
[S01] Vous essayez juste de rendre la vie plus difficile qu'elle est déjà.

43
00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:30.680
[S01] Mais un jour, vous réalisez que vous ne savez pas ce que vous voulez réellement.

44
00:02:30.990 --> 00:02:32.599
[S01] Vous savez ce qui ressemblerait bien.

45
00:02:32.759 --> 00:02:34.759
[S01] Vous savez ce qui ressemblerait impressionnant.

46
00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:38.280
[S01] Vous savez ce qui rend certains gens sourire avec l'approbation.

47
00:02:38.599 --> 00:02:41.639
[S01] Mais quand la vie devient paix et que personne ne claque,

48
00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:43.080
[S01] personne ne regarde,

49
00:02:43.479 --> 00:02:45.960
[S01] personne ne vous donne un signe que vous allez bien,

50
00:02:46.280 --> 00:02:48.919
[S01] quelque chose à l'intérieur semble étrangement vide.

51
00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:51.639
[S01] Et cette videsse n'est pas une faiblesse.

52
00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:53.080
[S01] C'est un message.

53
00:02:53.479 --> 00:02:56.599
[S01] C'est la partie de vous qui a été poussée dans le fond en demandant :

54
00:02:56.759 --> 00:02:58.199
[S01] "Quand arrivons-nous à vivre ?"

55
00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:01.479
[S01] Il y a un genre de prison qui n'a pas de mur.

56
00:03:01.719 --> 00:03:03.800
[S01] Elle est construite à partir de opinions imaginées,

57
00:03:04.039 --> 00:03:07.479
[S01] un regard, un commentaire, une réponse retardée,

58
00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:10.360
[S01] quelqu'un qui ne réagit pas comme vous l'espérait.

59
00:03:10.759 --> 00:03:13.800
[S01] Soudainement, votre état de colère tombe, votre confiance diminue,

60
00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:16.199
[S01] et votre esprit commence à travailler comme un détective

61
00:03:16.199 --> 00:03:19.159
[S01] à essayer de résoudre un crime qui peut même ne pas exister.

62
00:03:19.639 --> 00:03:20.919
[S01] "Ont-ils détesté moi ?"

63
00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:22.360
[S01] "J'ai dit trop ?"

64
00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:23.560
[S01] "Étrange ?"

65
00:03:23.719 --> 00:03:25.159
[S01] "Je me suis en retard ?"

66
00:03:25.879 --> 00:03:28.280
[S01] Ça sonne petit quand vous le dites en haut.

67
00:03:28.439 --> 00:03:33.000
[S01] Mais quand vous vivez de cette façon tous les jours, ça devient lourd, vraiment lourd.

68
00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:36.599
[S01] Focuser uniquement sur vous-même commence ici.

69
00:03:36.919 --> 00:03:39.479
[S01] Pas en arrogance, pas en froid,

70
00:03:39.719 --> 00:03:42.360
[S01] pas en prétendre que vous ne vous souciez pas de personne.

71
00:03:42.919 --> 00:03:46.360
[S01] Ça commence quand vous retenez le droit de définir votre propre vie.

72
00:03:46.759 --> 00:03:49.319
[S01] Vous arrêtez de demander : "Comment je me présente ?"

73
00:03:49.479 --> 00:03:51.800
[S01] Et vous commencez à demander : "Est-ce honnête ?"

74
00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:54.759
[S01] Vous arrêtez de demander : "Ils vont apprécier ?"

75
00:03:54.919 --> 00:03:59.080
[S01] Et vous commencez à demander : "Je peux respecter moi-même si je continue à vivre de cette façon ?"

76
00:03:59.560 --> 00:04:01.479
[S01] Cette question change tout,

77
00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:04.280
[S01] parce que l'approbation peut vous rendre sentir bien pour un moment.

78
00:04:04.599 --> 00:04:07.400
[S01] Mais le respect personnel vous donne du terrain sur lequel vous vous tenir.

79
00:04:07.879 --> 00:04:11.639
[S01] Une fois que vous commencez à voir à quel point votre énergie a été dépensée en jouant,

80
00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:14.039
[S01] un étrange désaccord peut apparaître.

81
00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:16.120
[S01] Vous pouvez vous sentir exposé,

82
00:04:16.279 --> 00:04:19.319
[S01] presque comme si vous enleviez un costume que vous portiez depuis des années

83
00:04:19.399 --> 00:04:21.399
[S01] et que votre peau ne connaît pas encore l'air.

84
00:04:21.879 --> 00:04:22.759
[S01] C'est normal.

85
00:04:23.319 --> 00:04:26.759
[S01] Les gens pensent souvent que la liberté devrait sentir itself bien,

86
00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:30.199
[S01] mais parfois, la liberté semble un peu étrange au début.

87
00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:36.040
[S01] Parfois, ça sent comme s'asseoir dans une pièce vide après que la musique arrête.

88
00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:37.639
[S01] Vous n'êtes pas perdu.

89
00:04:38.350 --> 00:04:40.680
[S01] Vous vous écoutez juste sans le bruit.

90
00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:43.160
[S01] Une masque n'est pas toujours une blague.

91
00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:06.649
[S02] Means the world can still speak, but it no longer owns your center.

92
00:06:07.199 --> 00:06:09.930
[S02] Someone can misunderstand you without destroying you.

93
00:06:10.589 --> 00:06:14.279
[S02] Someone can disapprove of you without making you abandon yourself.

94
00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:20.879
[S02] Someone can walk away, and yes, it may hurt, but it doesn't erase who you are.

95
00:06:21.569 --> 00:06:24.269
[S02] And from there, the journey goes deeper.

96
00:06:24.930 --> 00:06:30.540
[S02] Because once you stop living only through their eyes, another old habit tries to pull you back.

97
00:06:31.079 --> 00:06:32.850
[S02] It doesn't always come as fear.

98
00:06:33.389 --> 00:06:35.490
[S02] Sometimes it comes as comparison.

99
00:06:36.149 --> 00:06:42.779
[S02] You look around and wonder why others seem ahead, why their lives look cleaner, faster, more certain.

100
00:06:43.319 --> 00:06:46.529
[S02] And if you're not careful, you trade one cage for another.

101
00:06:47.069 --> 00:06:50.490
[S02] You stop performing for approval and start racing for worth.

102
00:06:51.329 --> 00:06:55.139
[S02] Comparison is sneaky because it pretends to be motivation.

103
00:06:55.589 --> 00:07:01.740
[S02] It tells you to look at other people so you can improve, so you can catch up, so you can become better.

104
00:07:02.430 --> 00:07:07.740
[S02] And sure, sometimes seeing someone else's discipline or courage can wake something up in you.

105
00:07:08.250 --> 00:07:09.360
[S02] Nothing wrong with that.

106
00:07:09.829 --> 00:07:14.220
[S02] But there's a darker kind of comparison, the one that doesn't inspire you.

107
00:07:14.670 --> 00:07:15.899
[S02] It humiliates you.

108
00:07:16.379 --> 00:07:20.579
[S02] It makes your own path feel small just because it doesn't look like someone else's.

109
00:07:21.389 --> 00:07:25.649
[S02] You see someone your age doing better, or at least appearing to do better.

110
00:07:26.129 --> 00:07:28.680
[S02] And suddenly, your whole life goes on trial.

111
00:07:29.490 --> 00:07:32.490
[S02] Their relationship becomes evidence against your loneliness.

112
00:07:32.939 --> 00:07:35.370
[S02] Their money becomes evidence against your effort.

113
00:07:35.879 --> 00:07:39.089
[S02] Their confidence becomes evidence against your uncertainty.

114
00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:42.089
[S02] Their timeline becomes a weapon in your own hands.

115
00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:48.839
[S02] And the saddest part is, you may not even want their life, not really, you just don't want to feel behind.

116
00:07:49.649 --> 00:07:50.639
[S02] But behind what?

117
00:07:51.029 --> 00:07:52.860
[S02] That's the question nobody asks.

118
00:07:53.220 --> 00:07:54.569
[S02] Behind whose schedule?

119
00:07:54.959 --> 00:07:59.069
[S02] Behind what invisible law that says your soul must bloom by a certain age?

120
00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:00.990
[S02] Heal by a certain season?

121
00:08:01.170 --> 00:08:03.000
[S02] Succeed by a certain deadline?

122
00:08:03.300 --> 00:08:05.519
[S02] Become impressive before anyone doubts you?

123
00:08:06.149 --> 00:08:10.829
[S02] A flower doesn't look at a mountain and feel like a failure because it isn't tall.

124
00:08:11.490 --> 00:08:14.790
[S02] A river doesn't apologize for taking the long way around stone.

125
00:08:15.540 --> 00:08:18.329
[S02] Nature understands something humans keep forgetting.

126
00:08:18.740 --> 00:08:22.860
[S02] Growth has rhythm, and rhythm can't be forced without breaking something.

127
00:08:23.490 --> 00:08:28.589
[S02] When you compare yourself constantly, you don't just envy another person's result.

128
00:08:29.040 --> 00:08:30.810
[S02] You betray your own process.

129
00:08:31.399 --> 00:08:37.019
[S02] You take the strange, winding, deeply personal path your life is trying to create.

130
00:08:37.399 --> 00:08:43.590
[S02] And you drag it into a marketplace where everything must be ranked, measured, displayed, and judged.

131
00:08:44.100 --> 00:08:45.840
[S02] And of course, you feel tired there.

132
00:08:46.440 --> 00:08:50.519
[S02] A sacred path cannot breathe in a place built only for competition.

133
00:08:51.240 --> 00:08:54.059
[S02] Focusing on yourself means leaving that marketplace.

134
00:08:54.419 --> 00:08:55.620
[S02] Not physically, maybe.

135
00:08:55.980 --> 00:08:57.330
[S02] You still live in the world.

136
00:08:57.629 --> 00:09:01.740
[S02] You still have responsibilities, goals, bills, people, work, dreams.

137
00:09:02.159 --> 00:09:04.440
[S02] But internally, something changes.

138
00:09:04.679 --> 00:09:08.039
[S02] You stop using other people's lives as a measuring tape for your own.

139
00:09:08.610 --> 00:09:12.690
[S02] You stop turning every success you see into a silent accusation.

140
00:09:13.409 --> 00:09:17.789
[S02] You begin to understand that someone else's sunrise doesn't mean your night is a mistake.

141
00:09:18.750 --> 00:09:22.889
[S02] There's an old saying, "A man who chases two rabbits catches neither."

142
00:09:23.370 --> 00:09:26.789
[S02] Simple, almost too simple, but painfully true.

143
00:09:27.389 --> 00:09:31.889
[S02] If your eyes are always on someone else's path, your feet can't fully walk your own.

144
00:09:32.309 --> 00:09:35.970
[S02] You'll keep changing direction based on what looks impressive from a distance.

145
00:09:36.389 --> 00:09:38.789
[S02] You'll pick up dreams you never actually wanted.

146
00:09:39.299 --> 00:09:42.750
[S02] You'll abandon quiet callings because they don't look dramatic enough.

147
00:09:43.409 --> 00:09:49.860
[S02] And years later, you may arrive somewhere that earns applause, but feels like a foreign country inside your own body.

148
00:09:50.700 --> 00:09:55.649
[S02] A person becomes dangerous, in the best way, when they stop needing to be ahead.

149
00:09:56.159 --> 00:09:59.159
[S02] Because then, they become difficult to manipulate.

150
00:09:59.700 --> 00:10:02.309
[S02] You can't shame them with someone else's timeline.

151
00:10:02.730 --> 00:10:05.220
[S02] You can't rush them with artificial urgency.

152
00:10:05.549 --> 00:10:09.539
[S02] You can't seduce them with every shiny version of success passing by.

153
00:10:10.019 --> 00:10:15.570
[S02] They may still work hard, maybe harder than before, but the work comes from alignment now.

154
00:10:15.899 --> 00:10:20.600
[S02] Not panic, not envy, not the need to prove they deserve to exist.

155
00:10:21.289 --> 00:10:23.190
[S02] That's when peace starts to return.

156
00:10:23.519 --> 00:10:27.659
[S02] Not lazy peace, not passive peace, a strong peace.

157
00:10:28.039 --> 00:10:32.970
[S02] The kind that says, "My path may not make sense to everyone, but it doesn't have to."

158
00:10:33.539 --> 00:10:38.129
[S02] And once that truth settles into you, comparison begins to lose its poison.

159
00:10:38.759 --> 00:10:40.529
[S02] You can admire without shrinking.

160
00:10:40.850 --> 00:10:42.509
[S02] You can learn without copying.

161
00:10:43.039 --> 00:10:46.159
[S02] You can celebrate someone else without turning against yourself.

162
00:10:46.350 --> 00:10:49.139
[S02] That's maturity, that's freedom with a spine.

163
00:10:49.850 --> 00:10:54.179
[S02] Yet even after comparison fades, something more subtle may remain.

164
00:10:54.570 --> 00:10:56.159
[S02] The fear of being judged.

165
00:10:56.539 --> 00:11:01.529
[S02] The feeling that people are watching, analyzing, silently deciding your worth.

166
00:11:01.970 --> 00:11:07.080
[S02] You may stop racing against others, but still feel haunted by their imagined opinions.

167
00:11:07.559 --> 00:11:12.029
[S02] So now the journey turns inward again, into a place most people avoid.

168
00:11:12.409 --> 00:11:16.950
[S02] Because it requires a kind of honesty that can feel uncomfortable at first.

169
00:11:17.539 --> 00:11:23.100
[S02] You begin to ask, "Are they really judging me, or am I hearing my own hidden voice through them?"

170
00:11:23.759 --> 00:11:27.330
[S02] Sometimes the biggest distraction in life isn't other people.

171
00:11:27.750 --> 00:11:30.570
[S02] It's the constant need to know what they think about you.

172
00:11:31.200 --> 00:11:37.379
[S02] You replay conversations, analyze reactions, and search for hidden meanings in every look or comment.

173
00:11:37.860 --> 00:11:40.830
[S02] Before long, your attention is no longer on your own path.

174
00:11:41.370 --> 00:11:43.649
[S02] It's trapped in a cycle of interpretation.

175
00:11:44.129 --> 00:11:50.129
[S02] And the more energy you spend trying to manage other people's opinions, the less energy you have for your own growth.

176
00:11:50.850 --> 00:11:55.289
[S02] The truth is, many of the fears we project onto others begin within us.

177
00:11:55.740 --> 00:11:59.759
[S02] If you secretly doubt yourself, every criticism feels larger.

178
00:12:00.330 --> 00:12:02.399
[S02] If you fear rejection, even

179
00:12:02.549 --> 00:12:03.940
[S03] Silence can feel personal.

180
00:12:04.500 --> 00:12:06.460
[S03] That doesn't mean your feelings aren't real.

181
00:12:06.909 --> 00:12:10.340
[S03] It simply means that not every battle is happening outside of you.

182
00:12:10.799 --> 00:12:14.860
[S03] Sometimes the real work is learning to recognize the voice inside

183
00:12:15.149 --> 00:12:16.830
[S03] that keeps questioning your worth.

184
00:12:17.470 --> 00:12:19.529
[S03] This is where real strength begins.

185
00:12:19.929 --> 00:12:22.059
[S03] Not by pretending nothing affects you,

186
00:12:22.399 --> 00:12:25.399
[S03] but by becoming aware of what affects you and why.

187
00:12:25.950 --> 00:12:28.830
[S03] Instead of reacting immediately, you pause.

188
00:12:29.500 --> 00:12:30.370
[S03] You observe.

189
00:12:30.779 --> 00:12:33.830
[S03] You ask yourself whether the situation is truly threatening

190
00:12:34.149 --> 00:12:36.029
[S03] or whether it's touching an old wound.

191
00:12:36.669 --> 00:12:39.490
[S03] That small moment of awareness can change everything

192
00:12:39.759 --> 00:12:43.149
[S03] because it shifts your focus from blame to understanding.

193
00:12:43.700 --> 00:12:45.500
[S03] As you spend more time with yourself,

194
00:12:45.830 --> 00:12:47.340
[S03] something starts to settle.

195
00:12:47.759 --> 00:12:49.370
[S03] The noise becomes quieter.

196
00:12:49.799 --> 00:12:53.029
[S03] The need for constant validation loses its grip.

197
00:12:53.629 --> 00:12:57.720
[S03] You stop chasing approval and start building trust in your own judgment.

198
00:12:58.149 --> 00:12:59.149
[S03] Little by little,

199
00:12:59.370 --> 00:13:02.370
[S03] your confidence stops depending on what happens around you

200
00:13:02.629 --> 00:13:05.149
[S03] and starts growing from what happens within you.

201
00:13:05.580 --> 00:13:07.580
[S03] That's when you become harder to shake.

202
00:13:08.250 --> 00:13:10.970
[S03] Praise is appreciated, but not required.

203
00:13:11.360 --> 00:13:14.149
[S03] Criticism is considered, but not worshipped.

204
00:13:14.750 --> 00:13:18.669
[S03] Other people's opinions become information rather than commands.

205
00:13:19.149 --> 00:13:20.340
[S03] You remain open,

206
00:13:20.600 --> 00:13:23.500
[S03] but you no longer hand over control of your identity.

207
00:13:24.059 --> 00:13:27.529
[S03] A person who knows themselves moves differently through life.

208
00:13:27.899 --> 00:13:30.629
[S03] They are not constantly seeking permission to exist.

209
00:13:31.090 --> 00:13:34.529
[S03] They are not changing direction every time someone disagrees with them.

210
00:13:35.090 --> 00:13:37.529
[S03] Their sense of worth comes from a deeper place,

211
00:13:37.899 --> 00:13:41.669
[S03] one that cannot be easily manipulated by approval or rejection.

212
00:13:42.370 --> 00:13:46.720
[S03] Focusing on yourself is ultimately about reclaiming your attention.

213
00:13:47.250 --> 00:13:51.029
[S03] It's about bringing your energy back from all the places you scattered it

214
00:13:51.320 --> 00:13:54.580
[S03] and investing it where it can actually create change.

215
00:13:55.250 --> 00:13:58.299
[S03] The more you do that, the more grounded you become.

216
00:13:58.799 --> 00:14:02.340
[S03] And the more grounded you become, the more untouchable you are.

217
00:14:02.700 --> 00:14:04.500
[S03] Not because nothing can affect you,

218
00:14:04.720 --> 00:14:07.340
[S03] but because nothing can take you away from yourself.
